  "solution": "For a quadratic equation of the form\n\n\\[\nat^2+bt+c=0,\n\\]\n\nthe product of its roots is given by Vieta’s formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Product of roots}=\\frac{c}{a}.\n\\]\n\nHere,\n\n\\[\na=18,\\quad b=45,\\quad c=-500.\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n\\text{Product of roots}=\\frac{-500}{18}\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{-500}{18}=-\\frac{250}{9}.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(-\\frac{250}{9}\\).",
